# TODO - Input and presentation contracts

## Objective

Protect shared controls and presentation behaviour.

## Acceptance

- Test keyboard, gamepad, hot-plugging and per-title touch configuration.
- Test responsive rendering, localisation and configurable frame pacing.

## Evidence

On 2026-11-24, `cargo validate --no-cache` passed after introducing
`games::input` and `games::presentation`. Synthetic input tests exercise
keyboard, gamepad device attach/detach, simultaneous held controls and
title-specific touch-zone mappings. Disconnection releases held buttons
without releasing an action still held by another device. Presentation
tests exercise landscape/portrait letterboxing, extreme viewport dimensions,
regional localization fallback and capped/uncapped frame interval policies.

The checks cover platform-neutral presentation contracts, not GPU output,
real physical devices or platform event-loop timing. Native integration
remains future platform work, and no actual game rendering is claimed.
